Ampere performance tuning for vLLM's Inkling 2 code, applied after apply_sm86_patch.py (patch -p1 --fuzz=0).
Measured on 2x RTX 3090 (sm_86): BENCH.md, "Tuning". Switch: INKLING_SM86_TUNE=all|none|<list> (README).

The small-matmul kernel tiles, the fused q/k/v launch, the loop-controller kernels, the drafter fold, the
draft-length range, the long-prompt attention loop and the one-kernel expert alignment are adapted from
snailbrainx/inkling-2-mini-sm80 (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/snailbrainx/inkling-2-mini-sm80).
Added here: the shared-memory fit for sm_86, the expert-GEMM kernel configs, router and attention tiles measured
on sm_86, the draft length chosen per step from recent acceptance (scheduler hook +
spec_decode/dynamic/adaptive_k.py), the reduced draft vocabulary (nvidia/dspark.py, speculator.py; its
ranking is patches/draft_vocab_rank.json), and the switches.

